This repository contains linguistic resources generated by the tools of the
Sanskrit Heritage Platform, applied to the Sanskrit Heritage Dictionary.

It contains 5 archives:

BOOK contains the current Sanskrit Heritage Dictionary as a PDF document.

DICO contains the current hypertext version of the Sanskrit Heritage Dictionary
as a set of HTML pages.

MW contains the hypertext version of the Monier-Williams dictionary aligned
with DICO. The yellow areas show the entries covered by Heritage.

DATA contains the linguistic data used by the Sanskrit Heritage Platform,
as Ocaml compressed persistent data files. 

CORPUS is the experimental corpus repository, containing the data available
by the Platform in the Corpus mode. 

The legacy XML dictionary used to contain XML data banks of Sanskrit forms 
given with their morphological taggings. These are produced mechanically 
by the declension and conjugation engines of the Sanskrit Heritage Platform, 
processing the Sanskrit lexicon underlying the Sanskrit Heritage Dictionary. 
Nowadays these data banks are computed at installation time of the Sanskrit 
Heritage Platform and down-loadable from a specific Sanskrit linguistic 
resources page, as explained in the Reference manual of the site. 

